From 57199a631b55c8ffe8fcccc00e2c036247f2a7bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 12:30:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Fix: tab content did not appear until a second activation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Clicking a memorial tab left the panel blank. The content only appeared
after pressing Enter, which re-fired the focused button and forced
another render.

CAUSE: both tab bars wrapped their panel in AnimatePresence mode="wait".
That mode deliberately holds the incoming child back until the outgoing
child's exit animation reports completion. Under React 19's concurrent
rendering that completion callback can be deferred indefinitely, so the
new tab never mounted and the panel stayed empty.

FIX: the panel is no longer gated on an exit animation. The incoming tab
mounts on the click and fades in; the outgoing one unmounts at once.
The 250ms fade with 8px rise is unchanged, so the transition looks the
same. AnimatePresence is retained where it is correct — the share modal.

Applies to every memorial: the shared MemorialTabShell (Virginia and all
future memorials) and John Peters' bespoke tab bar.

REGRESSION GUARD: added vitest + jsdom and four tests that click each
tab once and assert the content is on screen immediately, with no
waitFor and no second activation. Verified they fail on the unfixed code
and pass on the fix. Run with: npm test
