From 3986b0f6d2a083bbd70475a815d7dc65875e5f39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 16:54:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Fix: service provider panel crowded memorial content
 below 1280px
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 'Family Service Providers' panel sat BESIDE the memorial content on
every screen narrower than 1280px, squeezing the text and photographs
into an unreadable column. On a phone that meant two ~180px columns.

CAUSE: ServiceProviderRail renders two things — a sticky <aside> shown
only from xl up, and an inline <section> shown below xl. The containers
wrapping it were 'flex gap-12', a row at every width. So below xl the
aside correctly disappeared, but the inline section remained a flex
sibling of the content column and took half the width.

FIX:
- Four containers now stack by default and only become a row at xl:
  'flex flex-col gap-12 xl:flex-row'
    src/pages/MemorialPage.tsx          (all 22 dataset memorials)
    src/pages/john-peters/JourneyTab.tsx
    src/pages/john-peters/MemorialTab.tsx
    src/pages/john-peters/GlenTab.tsx
- ServiceProviderRail is now safe in any parent: full width when
  stacked, a fixed 280px column only from xl up.

Below 1280px the panel now sits cleanly BELOW the memorial content.
From 1280px up the sticky sidebar is unchanged.

Virginia's page was already correct — her rail renders outside the flex
row — so her layout is untouched.

REGRESSION GUARD: four tests, including a source check that any
'flex gap-12' in a file rendering the rail must also carry flex-col and
xl:flex-row. Verified they fail on the unfixed code. 14 tests pass.
---
