Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Provider rail: clear the sticky tab bar, and pin the
 layout with tests

The 'Family Service Providers' panel used sticky top-24 (96px) on every
page. On a memorial page the navbar (72px) and the sticky tab bar
(~48px, ~82px with sub-navigation) occupy up to ~154px, so on scroll the
panel slid underneath the tab bar and its top was covered. On the
/memorials directory there is no tab bar and 96px was correct.

New `belowStickyTabs` prop: top-[10.5rem] on pages with a tab bar,
top-24 on the directory. Applied to Virginia, the dataset memorial page,
and John's Journey, Memorial and Glen tabs.

Six regression tests pin the rules that keep this panel off the
memorial content: full width and stacked below xl, a fixed column only
at xl, sticky offsets that clear what is above them, parent layouts that
are flex-col until xl, and no z-index inversion in the sticky stack.

The responsive rules themselves were already correct in this repo. The
overlap being reported is on memoryglen-v3.vercel.app, which is a
different Vercel project and does not contain any of this work.
