From c67d4b5ec7d906b0f1654ce752a6b6762a251435 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 04:51:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Priority brief: homepage clarity, one family tree,
 mobile, Open Graph
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

P1 HOMEPAGE
- Hero: two calls to action only. 'View Demo Memorial' now lands on
  John Peters, a real populated memorial, not the directory.
- How it works cut from four steps to three, matching the brief.
- New 'What is a Family Glen?' section: one 38-word plain-language
  paragraph, before the term is used anywhere else on the page.
- Trust note answering the three questions people actually ask: who can
  see it, who controls it, how long it lasts.
- Order changed so the product is explained before it is shown off.

P2 FAMILY TREE — the data model was the root cause, as the brief suspected
The two trees had incompatible shapes. John's was x/y coordinates placed
by hand on an SVG canvas, with relationships implied by position;
Virginia's was four flat lists with no edges and no Glen membership.
Neither could express parent/child, spouse or multi-Glen reliably.
- New src/components/family/familyModel.ts: one normalised FamilyPerson
  with explicit generation, parentIds, spouseOf and glens.
- New src/components/family/FamilyTree.tsx: the single component, used
  on every memorial. Legend, generation labels, multi-Glen badge and
  note, loading/empty/error states.
- Generation rows that wrap, not a fixed canvas: readable at 320px with
  no horizontal scrolling and no pinch-zoom.
- Adapters map both memorials onto the model without changing their
  source data.

P3 MOBILE
- Every interactive element raised to at least 44px.
- Confirmed body text at 16px, tab bar scrolls rather than overflowing,
  tree stacks to one column.

P4 OPEN GRAPH — react-helmet would not have worked
This is a Vite SPA: one HTML file, everything drawn by JavaScript.
WhatsApp and Facebook do not run JavaScript when unfurling a link, so
tags injected at runtime are invisible to them and every memorial shared
as the generic site title.
- scripts/prerender.mjs writes a real static HTML file per memorial at
  build time with og:title, og:description, og:image, canonical and
  Twitter card tags. 29 pages. Wired into npm run build.
- WhatsApp share action added to memorial pages via wa.me.

15 new tests, one per requirement in the brief. 34 pass in total.
